IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `topca-minor`
IMPORT `topca-qa`

-- Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (topca-qa.l4): every exported question,
-- for every role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error
-- ("it is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own roles, with each value
-- under which the situation does not hold and every later input ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. Those cases
-- are generated from the exports' own parameter lists (the first section). For the young person (the baseline's seat)
-- the answers are also asserted equal to the baseline export's own answer on the same facts. The seller's and the
-- adult's answers are worked by hand from the text, and mirror cases ask the same facts from two seats. The items are
-- the baseline cases' own fixtures, copied unchanged (the baseline cases file is not imported, so its assertions are
-- not run twice).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked kind of item` IS A `Kind of item`
ASSUME `an unasked item` IS A `My item`
ASSUME `an unasked document` IS A `Kind of document`
ASSUME `an unasked finder` IS A `Who found me`

`as the young person` MEANS `I am under 18, and have or want tobacco, a smoking implement or a vape`
`as the seller` MEANS `I sell or supply tobacco products, smoking implements or vapes`
`as the adult` MEANS `I am a parent or other adult asked to buy, give or pass on tobacco or a vape for someone under 18`

`a vape` MEANS `a vaping product (a vape, pod, cartridge or vaping liquid, with or without nicotine)`
`a therapeutic vape` MEANS `a therapeutic vaping product (a vaping product that is a therapeutic good)`
`legal cigarettes` MEANS `a tobacco product (cigarette, cigar, loose tobacco or herbal smoking product) that meets the packaging and product requirements`
`illicit cigarettes` MEANS `an illicit tobacco product (one that breaks a tobacco product or packaging requirement)`
`a pipe` MEANS `a tobacco smoking implement (cigarette papers, rolling machine or pipe)`
`a lighter` MEANS `matches or a cigarette lighter`
`a candy cigarette` MEANS `a food, toy or other product designed to look like a tobacco or vaping product`

